Voting Unit (Unit A):
Included: All full-time, part-time and per diem* Nurse Case Managers residual to the existing registered nurse unit repesented by the Union, New York State Nurses Association, employed bythe Employer at its facility located at 4802 Tenth Avenue, Brooklyn, New York; 
Excluded: all guards and supervisors as defined in Section (11) of the Act.

*Per diem  employees eligible to vote are those employees  who have worked an average of four (4) hours or more per week during the 13 weeks immediately preceding the eligibility date for the election.

incl;
all full-time and regular part-time, per diem* registered nurses, temporary** RNs, including RN First Assists, Family Practice RNs, Clinical Systems Analyst RNs, Revenue Enhancement Specialist RNs employed by the Employer at its Somerville, NJ facility
excl;
Paramedic/Mobile Intensive Care Nurses, Employee Healthcare RN, team Leaders, Patient Advocate RN, Case employees, guards and supervisors as defined in the Act.

*  Who have worked an average of at least 4 hours per week in the calendar quarter preceding January 7, 2004.
